    {
      "cluster_id": 5,
      "headline_hint": "Parliament passes Anti-Paper Leak Bill amid Opposition walkout; PM hails law",
      "section": "india",
      "claim_count": 8,
      "distinct_outlets": 2,
      "source_kinds": {
        "fulltext": 8
      },
      "claims": [
        {
          "id": 44,
          "cluster_id": 5,
          "text": "The Rajya Sabha passed the Public Examinations (Prevention of Unfair Means) Amendment Bill, 2026, on Thursday after the Lok Sabha cleared it on Wednesday.",
          "kind": "event",
          "outlet": "The Hindu",
          "url": "https://www.thehindu.com/news/national/rajya-sabha-too-passes-bill-on-paper-leaks-opposition-walks-out-of-voting/article71287509.ece",
          "source_kind": "fulltext"
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "cluster_id": 5,
          "text": "Opposition members belonging to the INDIA alliance walked out of the Rajya Sabha prior to the government's reply on the Anti-Paper Leak Bill.",
          "kind": "event",
          "outlet": "The Hindu",
          "url": "https://www.thehindu.com/news/national/rajya-sabha-too-passes-bill-on-paper-leaks-opposition-walks-out-of-voting/article71287509.ece",
          "source_kind": "fulltext"
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "cluster_id": 5,
          "text": "Congress leader Mallikarjun Kharge stated that question papers for 152 state and central examinations were leaked over the past 10 years without offenders being punished.",
          "kind": "background",
          "outlet": "The Hindu",
          "url": "https://www.thehindu.com/news/national/rajya-sabha-too-passes-bill-on-paper-leaks-opposition-walks-out-of-voting/article71287509.ece",
          "source_kind": "fulltext"
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "cluster_id": 5,
          "text": "Under the amended law, individuals convicted of examination fraud face between five and 10 years in prison, compared with three to five years previously.",
          "kind": "figure",
          "outlet": "Livemint",
          "url": "https://www.livemint.com/news/india/pm-modi-drops-late-night-selfie-video-after-anti-paper-leak-bill-gets-parliament-s-nod-says-exam-mafias-wont-be-spare-11785440748411.html",
          "source_kind": "fulltext"
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "cluster_id": 5,
          "text": "The maximum financial penalty for individual offenders under the Anti-Paper Leak Bill was increased from ₹10 lakh to ₹50 lakh.",
          "kind": "figure",
          "outlet": "Livemint",
          "url": "https://www.livemint.com/news/india/pm-modi-drops-late-night-selfie-video-after-anti-paper-leak-bill-gets-parliament-s-nod-says-exam-mafias-wont-be-spare-11785440748411.html",
          "source_kind": "fulltext"
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "cluster_id": 5,
          "text": "Service providers involved in examination fraud face fines of up to ₹5 crore and can be barred from conducting examinations for 8 years.",
          "kind": "figure",
          "outlet": "Livemint",
          "url": "https://www.livemint.com/news/india/pm-modi-drops-late-night-selfie-video-after-anti-paper-leak-bill-gets-parliament-s-nod-says-exam-mafias-wont-be-spare-11785440748411.html",
          "source_kind": "fulltext"
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
